[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Authorship is one monotonic field, and it governs reversal rather than credit

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-AUTHORSHIP-LADDER
TITLE: Authorship is one monotonic field, and it governs reversal rather than credit
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: A reversal case appears that the four values cannot distinguish, or the ladder needs to run backwards.
STATEMENT: >>>
Authorship is tracked on every node, as ONE field on a MONOTONIC ladder, and
what it governs is REVERSAL rather than credit.

  llm            written by a model, not looked at
  llm-accepted   a human has seen it and let it stand
  llm-adopted    a human has taken it on as their own
  human          written by a human

The treatment reads off the value, three classes over four values:

  llm                          FREE. A model may reverse it without asking.
  llm-accepted                 SOFT. Undoing it is not a light choice, and an
                               undo has to surface in the report that closes
                               the work, so the human learns it changed.
  llm-adopted, human           HARD. A model may not reverse it. Being unable
                               to meet it is a STOP condition: raise it with
                               the human rather than working around it.

llm-adopted and human differ only in LINEAGE, which is why they share a
treatment. The ladder is one-directional: a value may rise and never fall, so
there is no reachability question and no way to launder a human commitment back
into a free one.

WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not attribution and not credit. It is the guard on the
reverse edge -- the answer to "who is allowed to undo this, and what do they owe
if they do." That is why it costs one field rather than an actor model: it
parameterises an undo that already exists instead of adding an axis.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The operator asked for authorship to be tracked even where nothing consumes it
yet, on the grounds that a view over it is interesting on its own and carrying
an unused field costs nothing. That is cheap to honour and expensive to
retrofit, since the value has to be recorded when the node is written and cannot
be recovered afterwards.

One field rather than two -- provenance plus a separate human stance -- because
only four of the combinations mean anything and they form a ladder. Two fields
would be a product with unreachable corners.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
The grammar today carries AUTHORED_BY with values llm and human only, and the sdoc writer refuses to set it at all -- MECH-RUNTIME-WRITE-GUARD makes it the operator's key. Extending the word list and deciding who may raise a value are both open, and the second is the harder one: raising to llm-accepted is a human act with no natural place to happen yet. The stop-condition and report-on-undo behaviour is semantic and belongs in L3, not in the field.
<<<
